-- Give Turtle's own uncommon, rare and epic gear a disenchant id
--
-- 1715 wearable weapons and armour pieces with entry 25000+ have
-- disenchant_id = 0, so disenchanting them fails with "Item cannot be
-- disenchanted" (Spell::CheckCast). Every target loot template already
-- exists in disenchant_loot_template; only the link on the item is missing.
--
-- These values are ESTIMATES, not data recovered from the live server.
-- They were derived by Shyalya (2026-08-02) from this project's own data:
-- for each quality, item class and five-point item level band, the
-- disenchant id most items already carrying one use. That reproduces the
-- standard vanilla tiers (uncommon armour 1-11, uncommon weapons 21-31,
-- rare 41-49, epic 61-65).
--
-- Deliberately NOT touched:
--   - entries below 25000 (original vanilla items). VMaNGOS agrees with this
--     project on all but one of them: the ones without an id are flagged
--     no-disenchant, deprecated, tokens, quest turn-ins or holiday items.
--   - items flagged ITEM_FLAG_NO_DISENCHANT (0x8000) or not wearable.
--   - PvP rewards (65 items): anything needing an honor rank, or
--     reputation with a battleground faction or the Bloodring (1008). Vanilla
--     flags its own PvP rewards no-disenchant, so these stay that way.
--   - reputation rewards (245 items): anything with required_reputation_faction
--     set, Turtle's own factions (Revantusk Trolls, Silvermoon Remnant, Wardens
--     of Time, Draenei Exiles, Earthen Ring, Dalaran - 165) and stock ones (80).
--     Vanilla flags 155 of its 160 uncommon-or-better reputation weapons and
--     armour no-disenchant, so a vendor-bought reward is not a cheap source of
--     enchanting materials. Turtle's intent for its own factions is unknown, so
--     they are left at 0 rather than guessed.
--   - quartermaster stock with no reputation requirement (2 items): Ancestral
--     War Totem (81199, Thunder Bluff Quartermaster, whose other stock all
--     needs Thunder Bluff reputation) and Basic Guide on Necromancy (81257,
--     Scourge Quartermaster). Unlimited stock at a fixed price, so treated as
--     the reputation rewards above.
--   - shirts and tabards (23 items, inventory types 4 and 19). They are
--     cosmetic, and vanilla has no disenchantable shirt or tabard at all.
--   - cosmetic and utility pieces (13 items) with no stats, armour, damage or
--     effect, or that are a tool rather than gear: the zero-armour "of the
--     Damned" plate set (80180-80186), Stormborn's Cape, Spring Chemise,
--     Flamewoven Ceremonial Mask, the quest props Slumbering Dreamveil and
--     Gemstone of Ysera, and the 7-day City Protector's Medallion teleport.
--
-- Only rows still holding 0 are changed, so this is safe to run twice and
-- never overwrites a deliberate value.

-- 18 items -> disenchant_loot_template 1
